## Mimic

Mimics are creatures out of fairy tale, made of an oily, corded substance and walking on four legs.

## Tzitzimitl

A tzitzimitl, called Sitzmittel in the tale, is a mimic-like creature of the cognitive side of the world. The tale tells of one that devoured whatever it met there before ever coming to the physical world, growing stronger with each thing it ate, until heroes came and killed it. They are said to be great spellcasters.

One was held in a case two feet on a side in the Office of Symbiotic Interactions of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]]. It is a mass of pinkish-red, oily, corded flesh, like a length of intestine, running and crawling about its case on many changing legs, sometimes eight, sometimes ten or twelve. Holy things wound it. When the case was lifted it filled with darkness and went cold to the touch, and it is now carried, case and all, in the [[Org/Althane/The Weft|Weft's]] bag of holding.
